   00001| //! Offline agentic driver — the in-repo "agentic CLI" that drives the server.
   00002| //!
   00003| //! This is the *client* side of issue #468's loop. The maintainer's framing:
   00004| //! *"our Formal AI system should have enough skills (meta algorithm, rust code) to
   00005| //! actually call all the tools from any agentic CLI, understand errors from tools,
   00006| //! and so on, call bash commands, do web fetch and web search, to actually
   00007| //! complete the task."* An external agentic CLI (link-assistant/agent, gemini-cli,
   00008| //! …) would normally play this role against our OpenAI-compatible server; this
   00009| //! module plays it in-repo so the whole loop runs offline and deterministically in
   00010| //! CI.
   00011| //!
   00012| //! It advertises a tool set, sends a chat request, and whenever the server answers
   00013| //! with `tool_calls` it **executes** each call — `web_search` / `web_fetch`
   00014| //! against the offline [`corpus`], `write_file` / `run_command` against a single
   00015| //! reused, sandboxed [`AgentWorkspace`] — feeds each result back as a `tool`
   00016| //! message, and loops until the server answers with `finish_reason: "stop"`. The
   00017| //! loop is bounded by a hard turn cap, so unbounded reasoning stays a NON-GOAL and
   00018| //! neural inference is never involved.
   00019| 
